WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.614 --> 00:00:02.110
(dramatic music)

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.955
- [Ta'u] I am where opera
and football collide.

00:00:04.955 --> 00:00:06.960
(singing in foreign language)

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.150
- [Minnie] Ta'u had a long journey

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:10.440
to the United States from Tonga.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.790
But his journey to center
stage in the opera house

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.069
took much longer.

00:00:14.069 --> 00:00:15.310
(singing in foreign language)
(crowd cheering)

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:16.840
- [Ta'u] My name is Ta'u Pupu'a.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.633
I am an operatic tenor.

00:00:19.721 --> 00:00:22.600
And I am an immigrant
from the Kingdom of Tonga.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.267
(dramatic orchestral music)

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:30.230
- My name is Minnie Driver.

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.960
I am an actress, a singer,
and I am an immigrant.

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.814
I believe nothing is more
American than its immigrants,

00:00:36.814 --> 00:00:39.130
so I'm teaming up with Great Big Story

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:43.043
to celebrate those that have
come here and left their mark.

00:00:44.382 --> 00:00:47.132
(dramatic music)

00:00:49.923 --> 00:00:52.506
(quirky music)

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:57.360
- When we moved to America,
I was seven years old.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.590
My parents wanted us nine
kids to have a education,

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.423
and so, America was the
land of opportunity.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:07.910
I started playing football when I was 10.

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:10.550
I was fast, I was strong.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.218
I knew that my vehicle into college

00:01:13.218 --> 00:01:15.443
was through playing football.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:21.390
- [Minnie] It turns out Ta'u
was a pretty good linesman.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:24.120
So good, in fact, that when
he graduated from college,

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:26.510
he was drafted by the Cleveland Browns,

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:28.260
but it was his taste in music

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:30.280
that often put him in the spotlight.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:31.540
- Before a game,

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:34.330
everybody's listening to
rock 'n' roll, heavy metal,

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:38.200
and I was the person on the
side listening to "O Sole Mio",

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.060
something to you know, inspire me.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:42.013
And then, I got injured and
I broke the arch of my foot

00:01:42.013 --> 00:01:43.560
and I didn't know what to do

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:46.281
because football was
the only thing I knew.

00:01:46.281 --> 00:01:48.600
A year later, I just that I decided that

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.313
I better follow my other love.

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:53.870
- [Minnie] So, Ta'u moved to New York

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:56.780
to pursue his other passion, opera.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.130
- I didn't know a single soul here.

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:01.140
I didn't know, like, how do
you become an opera singer?

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.700
The only thing I knew from my
playbooks and playing football

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.600
was you gotta have a plan.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.600
So I thought to myself,
well, to meet people,

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.930
if I get a job working in a restaurant

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:14.050
across the street from Juilliard,

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:18.240
you're gonna have operatic
singers, conductors coming in.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.590
- [Minnie] His plan worked.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.800
He met a man who helped
him secure an audition

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.980
at the Juilliard School of Music.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.080
- I got into Juilliard
on a full scholarship.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.050
I was sort of playing catch up

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:31.730
because my colleagues were
learning their solfeggio

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:34.643
when they were 17, 18 years old.

00:02:34.643 --> 00:02:38.725
(piano keys playing)
(Ta'u humming)

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.500
(singing in foreign language)

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.520
- [Minnie] And after three
years of rigorous training,

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.600
he graduated from Juilliard's top program.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.200
He has since traveled the
world singing in opera houses

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.840
and on concert stages.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:54.150
And today, among opera fans,
Ta'u Pupu'a is a big name.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.840
- I was blessed to run
around and sack quarterbacks,

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.653
and now I sing love songs to sopranos.

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:01.980
I like to live in the moment,

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.942
and my moment now is I am very happy

00:03:04.942 --> 00:03:06.818
to be an opera singer.

00:03:06.818 --> 00:03:10.310
(singing in foreign language)

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:13.290
To a young Polynesian that
is chasing their dreams,

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:18.290
set your goals high, dream
big, and make it reality.

00:03:19.137 --> 00:03:22.515
(singing in foreign language)

00:03:22.515 --> 00:03:25.765
(dramatic piano music)

00:03:27.512 --> 00:03:30.095
(bell echoing)

